"answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative aimed at enhancing security and accessibility, led by Marcus Cole. The project kicked off in July 2023 with a focus on leveraging AI for data visualization and secure file sharing. Key milestones include the approval of a $2M budget (later adjusted to $550,000 due to unforeseen expenses), the completion of the design phase, and the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype ahead of schedule. The team is expanding with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture, and a training budget of $15,000 has been approved for coding and management staff. Current phases involve development led by Omar Jensen and upcoming UI enhancements planned for October."
